From 7132909eec16f809e2c8e44c86dbc07d67c94c5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:58:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(app): face, trace and contour on imported meshes with
 float-noise corners

The #241 part (cutouts.camproj) is a closed mesh whose shared corners
scatter by up to 1.04 um and whose top stands 3e-13 mm uneven. Three
real failures on main, each a wrong refusal:

- slicer: chord ends welded by a rounded 1 um key split pairs that
  straddled a rounding boundary, so the closed part sliced "open"
  (12 dangling chord ends). Ends now weld within 2 um through a
  neighbourhood search (new geometry::slice_weld); a 0.1 mm gap still
  refuses as open.
- silhouette fallback: the facet-shadow union used Region::new's nesting
  parity, so bottom facets nested under top facets became phantom holes
  (27 on this part, up to 433 mm2) - a chain-only Face pick was clipped
  by them and refused on gaps that were not there. It is now a pure
  union (Region::union_all).
- section at Top of Part: a plane at the highest noisy corner met only
  that corner and read "no material". The section retries 1 um lower
  on an empty answer as it already did on an error; a plane that truly
  misses names the Z span to move Top of Part Z into.

The face-pick Facing "15.15 mm gap" refusal was #260, fixed by PR #313
(1da9695b). Box selection is filed as #979.

Pinned by an_open_mesh_rim_pick_faces_the_whole_top_with_no_phantom_holes,
sub_micrometre_corner_scatter_still_welds_into_a_closed_slice,
a_tenth_of_a_millimetre_gap_is_still_open,
a_whole_model_contour_at_a_noisy_top_sections_the_part and
a_top_plane_above_the_part_still_refuses_and_names_the_span.

Fixes #241

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
